title: |md
  # Withdraw FSM — states & transitions
  Solid = engine advances synchronously · Dashed = resumed by an external event
  Dashed-border state = pause (`_PENDING`, parks until an event)

  Screening is **one gate**, not the deposit's join and not a kyc
  gate before it: Abacus KYC-blocks a TARGET leg only, and a
  withdrawal debits the SOURCE, so a limits/KYC failure refuses the
  hold outright. This matches crypto-wallet's current hold path,
  where such a refusal fails the request and creates nothing.
| {near: top-center; width: 560}

direction: down

classes: {
  active: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {fill: "#EEF5FF"; stroke: "#6B9AE6"; stroke-width: 2; border-radius: 8}
  }
  pause: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {fill: "#FFF8E8"; stroke: "#D6A21B"; stroke-width: 2; stroke-dash: 4; border-radius: 8}
  }
  done_ok: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {fill: "#1E7A40"; stroke: "#1E7A40"; font-color: "#FFFFFF"; border-radius: 16}
  }
  done_bad: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {fill: "#B23B3B"; stroke: "#B23B3B"; font-color: "#FFFFFF"; border-radius: 16}
  }
  evt: {style: {stroke: "#2B6CB0"; stroke-width: 2; stroke-dash: 4}}
  sync: {style: {stroke: "#334155"; stroke-width: 2}}
}

start: "" {shape: circle; width: 18; height: 18; style: {fill: "#334155"; stroke: "#334155"}}

INTAKE_STARTED: {class: active}
SCREENING_AML_PENDING: "SCREENING_AML_PENDING\nawaits crypto-wallet's single verdict\nover its whole check chain" {class: pause}
DECISION_APPROVED: {class: active}
DECISION_REJECTED: {class: active}
FINALIZING_SEND_PENDING: "FINALIZING_SEND_PENDING\ncrypto-wallet sends on-chain (custody + Fireblocks)" {class: pause}
FINALIZING_COMMIT: {class: active}
FINALIZING_CANCEL: {class: active}
COMPLETED: {class: done_ok}
REJECTED: {class: done_bad}

start -> INTAKE_STARTED: "register\n(POST /withdrawal)" {class: sync}

# intake — create the Abacus hold that debits the user (user -> VOID).
INTAKE_STARTED -> SCREENING_AML_PENDING: "hold ok → ask CW to screen" {class: sync}
# A refused hold means no transaction AND no funds in flight: the user's balance is untouched, so
# ending the process is honest, not a swallowed incident. A limits/KYC refusal lands here too, which
# is what crypto-wallet's own hold path has always done with it.
INTAKE_STARTED -> REJECTED: "hold refused — no Abacus tx\n(no money, or limits/KYC declined)" {class: sync}

# the screening gate — the aml axis. CW runs its entire chain (repeated personal → shadow ban → repeated global
# → KYT via the AML service → significant) and reports ONE verdict; daedalus never sees the
# individual checks. NEEDS_REVIEW is a recorded sub-state, not a state: we keep waiting for the
# later approve/reject to arrive as a fresh verdict.
SCREENING_AML_PENDING -> SCREENING_AML_PENDING: "aml: NEEDS_REVIEW\n(need_kyc | manual | significant | shadow_ban)\n→ record aml in snapshot, keep waiting" {class: evt}
SCREENING_AML_PENDING -> DECISION_APPROVED: "aml: APPROVED" {class: evt}
SCREENING_AML_PENDING -> DECISION_REJECTED: "aml: REJECTED" {class: evt}

# decision -> finalization
DECISION_APPROVED -> FINALIZING_SEND_PENDING {class: sync}
DECISION_REJECTED -> FINALIZING_CANCEL {class: sync}

# the send pause: the hold stays held while CW drives custody. The on-chain result decides
# which way the hold resolves — commit only after the funds actually left.
FINALIZING_SEND_PENDING -> FINALIZING_COMMIT: "send result: SENT" {class: evt}
FINALIZING_SEND_PENDING -> FINALIZING_CANCEL: "send result: FAILED" {class: evt}

FINALIZING_COMMIT -> COMPLETED: "Abacus commit\n(funds leave the ledger)" {class: sync}
FINALIZING_CANCEL -> REJECTED: "Abacus cancel\n(hold reversed = funds returned)" {class: sync}

notes: |md
  **Notes**
  - statuses are the deposit's; the single gate reuses its `aml` axis
  - there is no kyc gate: `toTargetKycBlockedTransaction` blocks a
    TARGET leg only, and a withdrawal's account leg is the source
  - a refused hold is terminal here: no tx, no funds moved,
    nothing to unwind. A deposit must park instead (ACC #6)
  - no sendback pause: reversing the hold IS the return
| {near: bottom-center}
